## Wait for Compute Nodes

Wait for all compute nodes to become accessible via SSH.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Wait for compute nodes to be accessible -->
```bash
until pdsh -S -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" true \
	>/dev/null 2>&1; do
	echo "Waiting for compute nodes..."
	sleep 10
done
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

`sshd` answers before cloud-init has finished: its final stage still has to
write the munge key and run the `runcmd` restarts. Wait for it to complete on
every node, so that the resource manager steps below do not restart daemons
that cloud-init is restarting at the same time.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Wait for cloud-init to finish on the compute nodes -->
```bash
pdsh -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" cloud-init status --wait
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

If IPoIB is configured, check that it came up on every compute: NetworkManager
activates each node's connection once the interface and its InfiniBand link
appear.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify IPoIB on the compute nodes -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_ipoib -->
```bash
for ((t=0; ; t++)) ; do
	pdsh -S -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" \
		"nmcli -g GENERAL.STATE connection show ${ipoib_dev} | grep -qx activated" \
		>/dev/null 2>&1 && { echo "compute IPoIB: OK"; break; }
	(( t < 30 )) || { echo "compute IPoIB: FAILED"; exit 1; }
	echo "Waiting for IPoIB on the compute nodes..."
	sleep 10
done
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
